  "readmeFile": "Package.md",
  "releaseNotes": "4.0.0 — Breaking: ToolDefinition.Parameters is now Universal.Common.Json.JsonSchema instead of JsonElement (new direct dependency on Universal.Common.Json), so a schema is a real typed object graph instead of arbitrary parsed JSON -- construct it with `new JsonSchema { ... }` instead of JsonSerializer.Deserialize/JsonDocument.Parse of a string literal, and update any code that read td.Parameters via JsonElement's GetProperty/EnumerateArray to use JsonSchema's typed Properties/Required/Enum/Items instead. Tool<TArgs>.BuildParametersSchema() generates that schema directly from TArgs, instead of requiring a hand-authored literal kept in sync by hand -- the two could silently drift (a schema-advertised parameter name that doesn't match what ExecuteAsync actually deserializes) with nothing to catch it. Annotate TArgs with [JsonPropertyName]/[Description]/[Required] (or the C# `required` modifier); use a real enum for any closed set of values. Breaking: ArgsOptions now registers a JsonStringEnumConverter(JsonNamingPolicy.SnakeCaseLower) so enum-typed arguments deserialize from the same casing the generated schema advertises -- a subclass with an existing enum-typed TArgs property that relied on the previous numeric-by-default behavior needs to account for this.",
